# Walkthrough - Fixed Video Playback in Live Class Service

I have fixed the issue where the embedded video would not play when the play button was clicked in the Live Class Service.

## Changes Made

### 1. Fixed Component Shadowing
In [live-class-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/live-class-service.tsx), there was a local component named [LiveClassVideo](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/live-class-video.tsx#10-120) that was shadowing the imported component from `../components/live-class-video`. This local component lacked the state management and `onClick` handlers necessary for playback.

- **Action:** Removed the local [LiveClassVideo](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/live-class-video.tsx#10-120) definition.
- **Action:** Correctly imported and used the component from the `components` directory.

### 2. Added Subject Selection Logic
The page now tracks which subject is selected, allowing the main video to update when a subject card is clicked.

- **Action:** Added `useState` for `selectedSubject`.
- **Action:** Added `onClick` handlers to subject video cards.

### 3. Fixed Facebook Autoplay
Updated the Facebook video embed parameters to ensure it starts playing automatically when the user clicks the initial play button.

- **Action:** Changed `autoplay=1` to `autoplay=true` in [live-class-video.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/live-class-video.tsx).

## Verification Results

### Code Review
- [live-class-service.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/views/live-class-service.tsx) now correctly imports [LiveClassVideo](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/live-class-video.tsx#10-120).
- `selectedSubject` state is initialized to "Biology".
- Clicking on a subject card updates `selectedSubject`.
- [live-class-video.tsx](file:///c:/Users/User/Documents/monorepo-new/apps/home/modules/services/ui/components/live-class-video.tsx) now handles multiple subjects and uses the correct `autoplay` parameter.

### Manual Verification Required
Since this is a UI interaction with an external iframe, please verify:
1. Navigate to the Live Class Service page.
2. Click the large play button on the main video section.
3. Observe the Facebook video loading and playing.
4. Click on other subjects (Chemistry, Physics, etc.) and verify the main video section updates.
